CXR_VQA_RESULT={"status": "completed", "observation": {"answer": "Yes, there are signs of lung pathology present in this chest X-ray.\n\n*   **Consolidation:** There appears to be some increased opacity in the lower lung fields, particularly on the right side, which could represent consolidation. This is a dense area of fluid or inflammatory cells that obscures the underlying lung structures.\n\n*   **Effusion:** There is a blunting of the costophrenic angles, which could indicate the presence of a pleural effusion. Pleural effusions are collections of fluid in the pleural space, which is the space between the lung and the chest wall.\n\n*   **Edema:** There is some increased opacity in the lung fields, particularly in the perihilar regions, which could represent pulmonary edema. Pulmonary edema is the accumulation of fluid in the lungs.\n\nIt is important to note that this is just a preliminary assessment based on a single image. Further evaluation, such as a CT scan, may be necessary to confirm the diagnosis and determine the underlying cause of the lung pathology.\n\nDisclaimer: This analysis is for informational purposes only and should not be considered a substitute for professional medical advice. A qualified healthcare professional should be consulted for any health concerns.", "model": "google/medgemma-4b-it", "revision": "290cda5eeccbee130f987c4ad74a59ae6f196408", "backend_input_tokens": 297, "backend_output_tokens": 242}, "derived_images": [], "backend_compute_seconds": 18.59721310902387, "cuda_peak_allocated_bytes_by_visible_device": [9942664192], "original_image": "../../../assets/33ce8b09ee8e13191e62ad8c595622b5418dfbf2e91922f65d49325d279daa1e.jpg", "raw_result_file": "[REDACTED]", "clinical_correctness_verified": false, "actual_model_events": [{"kind": "generate", "model_class": "Gemma3ForConditionalGeneration", "module": "transformers.models.gemma3.modeling_gemma3", "status": "completed", "utc": 1794244925.2186286, "elapsed_s": 11.345650441013277}], "